.TH "YAMLR-EVIDENCE" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBExport Cryptographic Compliance Audit Evidence Bundle\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr evidence\fR command aggregates cryptographic manifest DNA fingerprints, Write-Ahead Log (WAL) remediation receipts, and engine environment states into a verifiable, auditor-ready evidence bundle archive.
.PP
This enterprise feature provides mathematical proof of manifest provenance, tamper-detection, and change tracking for SOC2, HIPAA, and CIS compliance audits.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Export evidence bundle for current workspace
yamlr evidence .

# Export bundle to custom tarball path
yamlr evidence ./k8s -o compliance-evidence.tar.gz

# Export evidence summary as structured JSON
yamlr evidence ./manifests --json
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.SS "Positional Arguments"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB[PATH]\fR: Workspace root or directory containing manifests and journals (defaults to \fB.\fR).
.SS "Output Controls"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-o, --output <PATH>\fR: Destination archive file path. Defaults to \fByamlr-evidence.tar.gz\fR.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-j, --json\fR: Emit evidence summary as structured JSON to stdout instead of packaging an archive.
.SH "EVIDENCE BUNDLE CONTENTS"
The exported bundle (\fB.tar.gz\fR) contains:
.PP
1. \fBRemediation WAL Journal\fR: Immutable event logs of every automated change applied by \fByamlr heal\fR.
.PP
2. \fBCryptographic DNA Fingerprints\fR: SHA-256 structural DNA records for before-and-after manifest states.
.PP
3. \fBAudit Results\fR: Findings from CIS benchmark and schema conformity checks.
.PP
4. \fBAttestation Metadata\fR: Timestamp, binary version, architecture, and operator identity.
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): Evidence bundle generated and exported successfully.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB1\fR (\fBEXIT_VIOLATIONS\fR): Violations or integrity discrepancies encountered during bundle assembly.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB124\fR (\fBEXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR\fR): File I/O or archive creation failure.
